{{also|allrounder|all rounder}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|all-arounder|all rounder}}

===Etymology===
From earlier {{af|en|all-round|gloss1=versatile|-er|id2=occupation}}, sense “versatile person” from 1875.<ref>{{R:Etymonline|all-round}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-all-rounder.ogg|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|chiefly|British}} A [[versatile]] person, able to do many things well; used especially in [[reference]] to being good at [[various]] sports. {{defdate|from 1875}}
# {{lb|en|cricket}} A [[player]] who is skilled in both [[batting]] and [[bowling]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author={{w|Shehan Karunatilaka}}|title={{w|Chinaman: The Legend of Pradeep Mathew}}|publisher=Jonathan Cape|page=26|passage=An '''all-rounder''' is a player who can bat and bowl. A genuine '''all-rounder''' should be able to make the team on either skill alone. A genuine one is as rare as a punctual Sri Lankan.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} A [[shirt]] [[collar]] going all round the neck and meeting in front.

